Package: corridoR
Title: Migration Corridors and Genetic Range Shifts from Landscape Genetic Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Paul A.", "Maier", , "maierpa@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0851-8827"))
Description: Tools for modeling genetic connectivity along migration
    corridors and forecasting how it shifts under climate change, following
    Maier et al. (2022) <doi:10.1038/s41437-022-00561-x>. Least cost
    corridors are built from accumulated cost surfaces and used as weights to
    summarize raw environmental layers between sites; each group of
    environmental features can choose its own corridor bandwidth; and
    pairwise predictions of differentiation and directional migration are
    mapped back onto the landscape as magnitude and net-direction surfaces.
    Includes readers for common genotype formats (STRUCTURE, GENEPOP, VCF,
    GenAlEx, FSTAT, PLINK, and 'adegenet' objects), pairwise FST, and the
    directional differentiation of Sundqvist et al. (2016)
    <doi:10.1002/ece3.2096>.
